Q1: What is a forEach loop?

A function-based loop used to run code for every element in a collection.

Q2: Can we use break or continue in forEach?

No, forEach cannot be stopped.

Q3: Difference between for-in and forEach?
for-in	forEach
simple loop	callback based
supports break	cannot break
no index	no index
works on list/set/map	works on list/set/map
Q4: Can we use forEach on maps?

Yes. map.forEach((key, value){})

Q5: Which one is cleaner for reading values?

forEach → shortest and cleanest.

Q6: When not to use forEach?

When you need index or break/continue.